    "summary": "Doll, male, of wood, the head and torso carved in one piece, both legs carved separately, articulated with flange hinges on iron pins; the hands are carved separately without arms, the parka sleeves being shrunk to fit tight over the wrists. The head is carved with slight features, and burnt hair. Seal-skin clothing consists of a parka, with the pointed tip characteristic of the male hood, and trousers, both items sewn with sinew and probably originally haired.",
